      "writtenOn": "2025-12-05T01:20:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not quite enough anymore to merely check if the page is mapped in the host EPT. For instance, IOMMU root/context/PASID/page tables are shared R/O with the host, i.e. they are obviously mapped in the host EPT, but we definitely don\u0027t want to allow the host to do DMA on those pages? (Well, we could allow it read-only DMA on them, but y\u0027know, that\u0027s not the point. 😊)\n\nSo we should check if the page state in the host EPT is PKVM_PAGE_OWNED?\n\n...So, I haven\u0027t looked into this and next patch very deeply yet, but it seems like it would be easier _and_ cleaner to implement all this generically as a part of mem_protect.c, perhaps similarly to pKVM-ARM\u0027s __pkvm_use_dma(). (Why easier - because mem_protect.c has __host_check_page_state_range(), at least.)",
      "revId": "dfb4a1d1c61b6ea549d4e28721a440115f0cd99a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
